# Copy to `.env` in this folder. Restart Metro after changes (`npx expo start -c` if URL sticks).
#
# ⚠️ Do NOT set EXPO_PUBLIC_API_* to Metro / dev server (http://172.x.x.x:8081) — Socket.IO will
# never reach Railway; chat will fall back to slow HTTP polling only.
# In __DEV__, `lib/api.ts` throws immediately if the resolved URL looks Metro-like (fix .env + rebuild).
#
# iOS dev client: values are baked into the native build — after changing .env run:
#   npx expo run:ios
# or `eas build --profile development --platform ios`, then npx expo start --dev-client -c
#
# Production (Railway) — set EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL (preferred) or EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE;
# embedded into the JS bundle at `eas build` / `expo export`. Matches `app.config.js` → extra.API_URL.
# Fallback if unset: `lib/api.ts` → https://cliniflow-backend-clean-production.up.railway.app
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE=https://cliniflow-backend-clean-production.up.railway.app
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://cliniflow-backend-clean-production.up.railway.app
#
# Local backend (same Wi‑Fi; use your Mac LAN IP, not localhost on a real phone):
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE=http://192.168.1.42:10000
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.42:10000
#
# Supabase Realtime (offer-thread chat — REQUIRED for live updates)
# Dashboard → Project Settings → API → Project URL + anon public key
# Uncomment and paste real values, then: npx expo start -c
#
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
